#!/bin/bash
# Installed in both application repositories on the secondary machine, by
# "Mark this as the secondary machine" in bootstrap.md. A plain `git push`
# skips both repositories' checks and records no tested pair, so ./deploy
# would refuse whatever it pushed. ./push, and ./deploy when it pushes its
# release tag, set FOODBANK_PROJECT_PUSH=1; nothing else should.
[ "${FOODBANK_PROJECT_PUSH:-}" = 1 ] && exit 0

cat >&2 <<'MESSAGE'
STOPPED: this is the secondary machine. Push with the project's push command, not git push:

    cd ..
    ./push

It runs both repositories' full checks, pushes the client and the server together and records
the pair it tested, which a deploy from this machine insists on. See secondary.md in the
project directory. Nothing was pushed.
MESSAGE
exit 1
